notes.content:
Greetings Swordsmen,

The Wandering Sword original soundtrack has been updated with new tracks from The Echoes of Ash and Dust update! Players who are interested can check it out and enjoy the new tracks!

We have also implemented several fixes and optimizations in this update. Here are the details:

[h3]New Features[/h3]
[list]
[*] Added a One-Tap Meridian Breakthrough function: When enough points are available, you can now fully upgrade any meridian by selecting an acupoint and tapping the One-Tap Breakthrough button to the left of the original breakthrough button;
[*] Added recovery elixirs: The Wudang Sect disciple Yuan Ji, located to the right of Dao Xuan, now sells three types of elixirs – Primordial Elixir, Celestial Elixir, and Supreme Yin-Yang Elixir; these elixirs restore minor, major, or all Qi and True Qi, respectively;
[*] Added a new setting option allowing players to decide whether the Overcomer and Apex Challenger difficulty expansions apply in ally-only battles;
[*] Added a new lightness skill to the Tianji Legacy: Star-Treading Steps;
[/list]

[h3]Fixes and Optimizations[/h3]
[list]
[*] Fixed missing collision in Buddha’s Hollow;
[*] Enhanced the skill Xuanxu Saberplay, with slightly improved effects;
[*] Fixed an issue with the quest "Challenge Chenghuang Illusion and Comprehend Evergreen Vitality Mastery," which remained marked as incomplete after the challenge was completed;
[*] Unified skill and buff descriptions for "critical resistance," replacing all instances of "anti-critical" or similar terms with Critical Resistance;
[*] Modified the first battle in the main storyline journey to Xuanhuo Cult to end after 5 turns;
[*] Optimized the chest placement near the suspension bridge on Mount Windless to prevent character blockage;
[*] Adjusted the side quest "Yuanqi of Wudang" to be unclaimable after entering the Echoes of Dust main storyline;
[*] Added a prompt during Echoes of Dust storyline entry, preventing teammates from leaving or joining the team;
[*] Fixed a bug where repeatedly entering the grove could trigger the Yao Ji CG encounter;
[*] Adjusted the unlocking condition for Jiang Xiaotong in the companion guide. Now, visiting Jiang Xiaotong will also unlock her profile;
[*] Resolved an issue in the old main storyline where killing Mo Wen solo would trigger the companion ending repeatedly;
[*] Fixed a map error with the Ouyang Xue CG in Qingxiao Line after defeating Mo Wen together with Xuanhuo Cult;
[*] Resolved a bug in the tutorial’s Yuwu Branch where, after Cheng Wanqing’s death, interacting with her did not grant the Eight Trigrams of Roving Tiger skill manual (players who meet the conditions can collect it from Cheng Yu);
[*] Addressed a bug preventing entry into the Wudang Forbidden Area before heading to Buddha’s Hollow in the main storyline if Cloudform Tai Chi was not previously completed;
[*] Extended the combat duration for the initial encounter with Zhao An at Pili School from 10 to 15 turns;
[*] Fixed missing walking sound effects;
[*] Corrected a sorting bug in the consumables section;
[*] Improved the guide unlocking process: Guides with multiple branches can now be unlocked by completing any one of them;
[*] Adjusted the effects of Cloud-Capped Leap:
- Level 1 Effect – Added a new attribute: "All Wudang Sect moves deal 15% more damage for 2 turns after use."
- Level 5 Effect – Added a new attribute: "Adds 2-3 layers of Agility per turn during Cloud-Capped Leap."
[/list]

If you encounter any issues or bugs during your journey, feel free to leave comments in our Steam discussion area or on our bug report form. We’ll continue working hard to bring you an even better gaming experience!

https://store.steampowered.com/app/1876890/Wandering_Sword/

That’s all for today’s update! And finally, don’t forget to follow us on Steam and Twitter for the latest announcements! 

